@*
    Views/Home/Privacy.cshtml — the privacy & cookies page (/Privacy).
    Linked from the cookie notice (Views/Shared/_CookieNotice.cshtml) and the footer.
    Keep the cookie table in step with the code if cookies are added or removed:
    Program.cs (admin login), the admin forms (antiforgery) and
    AdminControllerBase.SetMessage (TempData).
*@
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy & cookies";
}

<div class="page-header">
    <p class="page-eyebrow">Privacy</p>
    <h1>Privacy & cookies</h1>
</div>

<article class="post-article post-article--page">
    <div class="post-body prose page-card">
        <p><strong>In short: this site does not track you.</strong>
            There are no analytics, no ads and no cookies from other companies.</p>

        <h2>Cookies</h2>
        <p>A cookie is a small text file the site stores in your browser. Visitors get no cookies at all;
            the ones below are only used in the admin area, by the site owner:</p>

        <table>
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th scope="col">Cookie</th>
                    <th scope="col">Purpose</th>
                    <th scope="col">Kept for</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr>
                    <td><code>PersonalSite.Admin</code></td>
                    <td>Keeps the site owner logged in to the admin area. Does not affect visitors.</td>
                    <td>8 hours of inactivity</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><code>.AspNetCore.Antiforgery.*</code></td>
                    <td>Protects the login and admin forms against attacks from other websites.</td>
                    <td>Until the browser closes</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><code>.AspNetCore.Mvc.CookieTempData</code></td>
                    <td>Shows a confirmation message in the admin area after something is saved.</td>
                    <td>Deleted once the message is shown</td>
                </tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>

        <p>Because these cookies are needed for features you use yourself, no consent is required. When you click OK on the cookie notice, that is saved in your browser's local storage (not as a cookie), so the notice doesn't show again.</p>

        <h2>Fonts from Google</h2>
        <p>The site's fonts (Playfair Display and Inter) are loaded from Google Fonts. That sets no cookies, but your browser contacts Google's servers, which therefore see your IP address.</p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>Questions about your privacy? Write to
            <a href="mailto:bjarne@lundqwist.se">bjarne@lundqwist.se</a>.</p>
    </div>
</article>
